{"repositoryId":1219554318,"availability":"available","full":"obataka/temporal-demo","name":"temporal-demo","description":"Fault-tolerant multi-agent AI workflows with Temporal — durable state, explicit retry policy, and hard human-approval gates via CrewAI.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":1,"created":"2026-04-24T01:52:41Z","updated":"2026-08-07T01:49:41Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://project-sy5bk.vercel.app","topics":["agentic-ai","ai-agents","crewai","distributed-systems","durable-execution","fault-tolerance","human-in-the-loop","llm","multi-agent-systems","python","retry-policy","temporal","temporal-io","workflow-engine","workflow-orchestration"],"demo":"https://project-sy5bk.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T13:45:56.128Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T13:45:56.128Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T13:45:56.128Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T13:45:56.128Z","stars":0,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A reference implementation for running multi-agent LLM systems under hard human-approval gates — built on Temporal for durable state and explicit retry policy.","Most \"AI agent\" demos share three properties that make them unfit for production: they hold state in process memory, they treat human approval as an optional UI affordance rather than a hard gate, and they have no answer for what happens when a call to the LLM provider times out at 2am. In a real deployment, approval waits legitimately span days, LLM calls fail routinely on rate limits and transient errors, and Human-in-the-Loop cannot be implemented as polling without inheriting the failure modes of a distributed system you never admitted to building. This repository is a reference…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/obataka/temporal-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c2385b9d0d2ab44b5a4bb6c55d0b2e5f8e4be3fc145345280e5b3250e82f4dea","extracted